steps:
1. Create src/components/blog/Breadcrumbs.tsx
   Props: { category: string; categorySlug: string; articleTitle: string }
   Implementation: use the existing Breadcrumb/BreadcrumbList/BreadcrumbItem/BreadcrumbLink/BreadcrumbPage/BreadcrumbSeparator primitives from @/components/ui/breadcrumb. Render: Home › Articles & Blog › {category} › {articleTitle}. Home links to '/', Articles & Blog links to '/blog', Category links to '/blog' with a search param (or just /blog for now). Wrap in a <nav> with bg-cream border-b border-border. Container-rhl padding. Text size sm.

3. Create src/components/blog/FeatureMedia.tsx
   Props: { src: string; alt: string; overlayText?: string }
   Implementation: a full-width image block, rounded-xl overflow-hidden mt-6. <img loading='lazy' src={src} alt={alt} className='w-full aspect-[16/7] object-cover'/>. If overlayText is provided, render it as an absolute-positioned white text overlay at the bottom with a dark gradient. The component itself does not constrain width — the parent layout controls that.

5. Create src/components/blog/BottomLineCallout.tsx
   Props: { text: string }
   Implementation: a rounded-xl box with bg-accent border border-primary/30 p-6 mt-10. Leading icon: Leaf from lucide-react (text-primary h-5 w-5). Heading: 'The Bottom Line' in font-semibold text-primary. Body text below. Only rendered when text prop is non-empty.

6. Create src/components/blog/RecentArticles.tsx
   Props: { currentSlug: string; posts: BlogPost[] }
   Implementation: takes the full post list, filters out currentSlug and published=false, sorts by date descending, takes the first 4. Renders a compact list: each item is flex gap-3. Left: 48px square image (<img loading='lazy'> or a green initial placeholder if no featureImageUrl). Right: title (font-semibold text-sm line-clamp-2, Link to /blog/$slug) + date (text-xs text-muted-foreground). 'View All →' link at bottom to /blog.

9. Create src/components/blog/TopicExplorer.tsx
   Props: { categories: { slug: string; label: string; icon: string }[] }
   Implementation: card wrapper rounded-xl border border-border bg-card p-5. Heading 'Explore More Articles' font-semibold mb-3. Two-column grid (grid-cols-2 gap-2). Each item: Link to /blog with a search param (or just /blog for now). flex items-center gap-2. Small Lucide icon (use a lookup map: Heart, Leaf, Shield, Apple, Activity, Brain, Pill, Moon mapped to known categories; default to BookOpen). Text text-sm. Touch target min-h-[44px].

10. Create src/components/blog/RecommendedProducts.tsx
    Props: { productSlugs: string[]; categoryLabel?: string }
    Implementation: reads productSlugs, looks each up in the catalogProducts array imported from @/data/catalog (use the `catalogProducts` export — check catalog.ts carefully; it may be named differently, verify during implementation). Renders only products that exist in the catalog. Full-width section, NOT inside the sidebar. Heading 'Recommended for You' (or 'Recommended Products'). Horizontal scroll on mobile, 4-column grid on desktop (grid-cols-2 sm:grid-cols-4). Each card: rounded-xl border border-border bg-card p-4. Product image 80px (placeholder from assets if no dedicated image). Product name font-semibold text-sm. Short support statement text-xs text-muted-foreground mt-1 line-clamp-2. 'Learn More →' as a Link to /products/$slug. 'View All {categoryLabel} Products →' link below the grid.

11. Create src/components/blog/ReferencesAccordion.tsx
    Props: { references: ArticleReference[] }
    Implementation: uses Accordion/AccordionItem/AccordionTrigger/AccordionContent from @/components/ui/accordion. Single item, default closed. Trigger: 'References & Sources ({count})'. Content: ordered list ol. Each reference: li with title in font-medium, authors/publisher/year in text-sm text-muted-foreground. If url present, wrap title in <a href={url} target='_blank' rel='noopener noreferrer' className='hover:text-primary underline'>. Only rendered if references.length > 0.

12. Create src/components/blog/DisclaimerAccordion.tsx
    Props: { text: string }
    Implementation: same Accordion primitives. Single item, default closed. Trigger: 'Health & Educational Disclaimer'. Content: text-sm text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed. This is always rendered — the parent must always pass GLOBAL_DISCLAIMER.

13. Create src/components/blog/RelatedArticles.tsx
    Props: { slugs: string[]; allPosts: BlogPost[] }
    Implementation: maps slugs to posts (filters undefined and unpublished). Renders a row (grid-cols-2 on mobile, grid-cols-4 on desktop). Each card: rounded-xl border border-border bg-card overflow-hidden. Top image area: featureImageUrl or colored placeholder. Title Link to /blog/$slug font-semibold text-sm line-clamp-2. Date text-xs text-muted-foreground. 'View All Articles →' link at section heading level.

15. Create src/components/blog/ArticleSidebar.tsx
    Props: { post: BlogPost; allPosts: BlogPost[] }
    Implementation: a <aside> with flex flex-col gap-6. Renders RecentArticles, NewsletterSubscribe, U20XPromo, TopicExplorer in that order. Passes post.u20xChallengePath ?? '/u20x' to U20XPromo ctaPath. Passes ARTICLE_CATEGORIES to TopicExplorer. This component is sidebar-only (hidden on mobile via lg:flex — the parent layout handles the sticky/column behavior).
